---
// The path of one agent run, from the coding agent to the run page. Top to bottom so it stays readable on a phone.
// Colours come from currentColor and Starlight's --sl-color-* variables, so it follows the light and dark themes.
---

<figure class="inspection-flow">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 360 500" role="img" aria-labelledby="inspection-flow-title inspection-flow-desc">
    <title id="inspection-flow-title">The path of an agent run</title>
    <desc id="inspection-flow-desc">
      1, the coding agent sends spans and log records over OTLP/HTTP to port 4318 with the send-only collector token. 2, your
      collector checks the token, redacts and batches, then writes with the store writer credential. 3, your store holds the
      telemetry. 4, ShipLean reads the store with its own read-only user and shows the run on the item. Nothing flows from the
      agent or the collector to ShipLean.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="inspection-flow-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="currentColor"></path>
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <g class="box">
      <rect x="4" y="4" width="352" height="78" rx="8"></rect>
      <circle cx="30" cy="30" r="14"></circle>
      <text class="num" x="30" y="35">1</text>
      <text class="name" x="54" y="35">Coding agent</text>
      <text class="sub" x="54" y="56">Claude Code, Codex CLI or Cursor</text>
      <text class="sub" x="54" y="73">on a developer's machine or CI runner</text>
    </g>

    <line class="flow" x1="40" y1="84" x2="40" y2="140" marker-end="url(#inspection-flow-arrow)"></line>
    <text class="label" x="58" y="106">spans and log records, OTLP/HTTP</text>
    <text class="label" x="58" y="124">port 4318, send-only collector token</text>

    <g class="box">
      <rect x="4" y="142" width="352" height="78" rx="8"></rect>
      <circle cx="30" cy="168" r="14"></circle>
      <text class="num" x="30" y="173">2</text>
      <text class="name" x="54" y="173">Collector (yours)</text>
      <text class="sub" x="54" y="194">checks the token, redacts,</text>
      <text class="sub" x="54" y="211">batches, writes to the store</text>
    </g>

    <line class="flow" x1="40" y1="222" x2="40" y2="278" marker-end="url(#inspection-flow-arrow)"></line>
    <text class="label" x="58" y="254">store writer credential</text>

    <g class="box">
      <rect x="4" y="280" width="352" height="78" rx="8"></rect>
      <circle cx="30" cy="306" r="14"></circle>
      <text class="num" x="30" y="311">3</text>
      <text class="name" x="54" y="311">Store (yours)</text>
      <text class="sub" x="54" y="332">ClickHouse, or Tempo (traces)</text>
      <text class="sub" x="54" y="349">and Loki (logs)</text>
    </g>

    <line class="flow" x1="40" y1="416" x2="40" y2="360" marker-end="url(#inspection-flow-arrow)"></line>
    <text class="label" x="58" y="384">ShipLean reads with its own</text>
    <text class="label" x="58" y="402">read-only user</text>

    <g class="box">
      <rect x="4" y="418" width="352" height="78" rx="8"></rect>
      <circle cx="30" cy="444" r="14"></circle>
      <text class="num" x="30" y="449">4</text>
      <text class="name" x="54" y="449">ShipLean</text>
      <text class="sub" x="54" y="470">Agent runs on the item,</text>
      <text class="sub" x="54" y="487">and the run page</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
</figure>

<style>
  .inspection-flow {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }
  .inspection-flow svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 30rem;
    height: auto;
  }
  .box rect {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
    stroke: var(--sl-color-accent);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .box circle {
    fill: var(--sl-color-accent);
  }
  .num {
    fill: var(--sl-color-black);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .name {
    fill: var(--sl-color-white);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .sub {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .flow {
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .label {
    fill: currentColor;
    font-size: 12.5px;
  }
</style>
